{
  "format": "srwb",
  "version": "1.0",
  "notebook": {
    "name": "Flooded-Mine Cooling: Water–Energy Trade-offs",
    "cells": [
      {
        "code": "# Flooded-Mine Cooling: Water–Energy Trade-offs\n\n*A fictional educational toy model—not an engineering design, site assessment, financial analysis, or measured performance claim.*\n\nA nominal **10 MW liquid-cooled data center** (a 9–10 MW illustrative hourly load) rejects heat through an induced-draft evaporative cooling tower. A plenum routes the warm exhaust over a condenser coil connected to a flooded-mine thermal reservoir. Recovered condensate can replace part of the tower's makeup water. Separate water circuits exchange heat without mixing.\n\n## Run order and requirements\n\nRun the code cells from top to bottom: **simulation → classification → dashboard → dry_cooling → analysis_plots**. SciREPL provides NumPy, Plotly's `mplot` helper, the shared filesystem, and the named-cell `nb_read`/`nb_write` APIs. The Python simulation writes local CSV/fact files under `/shared` and updates only the named `classification` cell. No workbook code calls an external service or AI provider. Initial runtime installation may require a download in editions without bundled kernels.\n\n## What is assumed\n\nThe mine is one perfectly mixed reservoir with a constant recharge coefficient; there is no stratification, groundwater-flow model, seasonal weather, water chemistry, health assessment, or tower-control optimization. The coil's UA/effectiveness formula supplies a **toy heat-transfer budget**, not a calibrated wet-coil design. Its outlet temperature and condensation are then solved together using total moist-air enthalpy, including the enthalpy carried away by condensate. That same heat transfer warms the mine.\n\nThe heat-pump COP, fans, pumps, dry-cooler approaches, grid-water factors, and classification thresholds are declared assumptions. The heat-pump operating point is recalculated once rather than fully iterated. A single hot week is multiplied by weeks per year only for a **same-weather comparison**, not an annual forecast. The dry-cooling comparison uses the hot-dry case only.\n\nThe water metric combines site tower makeup (evaporation, drift and blowdown) with attributed electricity-generation consumption. Blowdown return flows are not modeled, so this sum is an illustrative accounting metric, not a consistent water-consumption footprint.\n\nInspect the assumptions, energy-balance residuals, units, and sensitivity plots before interpreting the results. A cold reservoir below the plume's dew point is necessary for condensation, but is not by itself proof of feasible equipment or long-term water savings.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "intro"
      },
      {
        "code": "import numpy as np, csv\n\n# ============ ILLUSTRATIVE CONSTANTS (toy model, no false precision) ============\nP_ATM  = 101.3          # kPa atmospheric pressure\nHOURS  = 168            # one week, hourly\nDT     = 3600.0         # s per hour\nCP_W   = 4.186          # kJ/kg-K water\nCP_A   = 1.006          # kJ/kg-K dry air\nIT_MEAN, IT_AMP = 9.5, 0.5        # MW IT load diurnal schedule (both cases)\nT_MEAN,  T_AMP  = 32.0, 7.0       # degC dry-bulb diurnal schedule (both cases)\nRH_SCHED = {'hot_dry': (27.5, 7.5), 'hot_humid': (65.0, 10.0)}  # % mean, amp\n\nTOWER_EFF  = 0.70       # constant tower effectiveness\nAIR_PER_MW = 55.0       # kg dry-air/s per MW IT (induced-draft fan schedule)\nM_WATER    = 420.0      # kg/s tower water design flow\nCOC        = 5.0        # cycles of concentration\nDRIFT_FRAC = 2.0e-5     # drift as fraction of circulating water\nFAN_ETA, COIL_DP, RHO_AIR = 0.6, 50.0, 1.15   # fan eff., coil pressure drop Pa\n\nT_FAC_LIMIT = 27.0      # degC illustrative facility supply limit (W27-class)\nHX_APPROACH = 3.0       # K heat-exchanger approach\n\nCOIL_UA   = 600.0       # kW/K fixed, widely spaced finned-tube coil\nCOIL_APP  = 2.0         # K coil-surface approach above mine water\nM_MINE    = 100.0       # kg/s mine-loop flow\nPUMP_HEAD, PUMP_ETA = 15.0, 0.75\nT_MINE0, T_ROCK = 12.0, 12.0      # degC mine start / far-field rock\nV_MINE    = 3.0e5       # m3 effective reservoir volume\nU_LOSS    = 200.0       # kW/K recharge/loss to rock and groundwater\n\n# ============ PSYCHROMETRICS ============\ndef psat(T):            # saturation vapour pressure, kPa (Magnus/Alduchov-Eskridge)\n    return 0.61094*np.exp(17.625*T/(T+243.04))\ndef w_of(T, RH):        # humidity ratio kg/kg dry air\n    pv = RH/100.0*psat(T); return 0.62198*pv/(P_ATM-pv)\ndef w_sat(T): return w_of(T, 100.0)\ndef tdp_of_w(w):        # dew point from humidity ratio, degC\n    pv = w*P_ATM/(0.62198+w); a = np.log(pv/0.61094)\n    return 243.04*a/(17.625-a)\ndef twb_stull(T, RH):   # wet bulb, Stull (2011) empirical approximation\n    RH = np.clip(RH, 1.0, 100.0)\n    return (T*np.arctan(0.151977*(RH+8.313659)**0.5) + np.arctan(T+RH)\n            - np.arctan(RH-1.676331) + 0.00391838*RH**1.5*np.arctan(0.023101*RH) - 4.686035)\ndef h_air(T, w):        # moist-air enthalpy kJ/kg dry air\n    return CP_A*T + w*(2501.0 + 1.86*T)\n\ndef plume(Tdb, RH, Q_kw, m_air):\n    \"\"\"Captured nearly-saturated tower exhaust via moist-air energy balance (bisection).\"\"\"\n    w_in = w_of(Tdb, RH)\n    h_t  = h_air(Tdb, w_in) + Q_kw/m_air\n    lo, hi = twb_stull(Tdb, RH), 60.0\n    for _ in range(40):\n        mid = 0.5*(lo+hi)\n        if h_air(mid, 0.98*w_sat(mid)) < h_t: lo = mid\n        else: hi = mid\n    Tp = 0.5*(lo+hi); w_p = 0.98*w_sat(Tp)\n    return w_in, Tp, w_p, tdp_of_w(w_p)\n\ndef plume_condenser(Tp, w_p, Tm, m_air):\n    \"\"\"Energy-limited toy coil, not a calibrated wet-coil/geometry model.\n\n    Moist-air enthalpy uses a 0 degC liquid-water reference. Condensate\n    leaves at outlet air temperature, so its liquid enthalpy is subtracted.\n    Return total heat to the mine, outlet temperature/humidity, total\n    condensation, and the energy-balance residual.\n    \"\"\"\n    if m_air <= 0.0:\n        raise ValueError(\"The illustrative coil requires positive airflow\")\n    surface = Tm + COIL_APP\n    if Tp <= surface:\n        return 0.0, Tp, w_p, 0.0, 0.0\n\n    def outlet(T):\n        w_out = min(w_p, w_sat(T))\n        condensed = m_air * max(0.0, w_p - w_out)\n        total_heat = (m_air * (h_air(Tp, w_p) - h_air(T, w_out))\n                      - condensed * CP_W * T)\n        return total_heat, w_out, condensed\n\n    # Retain a simple UA-based heat-transfer budget. Explicitly cap it\n    # by the air-side approach limit and mine-loop heat capacity.\n    c_min = min(m_air * (CP_A + 1.86 * w_p), M_MINE * CP_W)\n    eff_c = 1.0 - np.exp(-COIL_UA / c_min)\n    budget = eff_c * c_min * (Tp - surface)\n    max_air, _, _ = outlet(surface)\n    max_water = M_MINE * CP_W * (Tp - surface)\n    target = max(0.0, min(budget, max_air, max_water))\n    lo, hi = surface, Tp\n    for _ in range(50):\n        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n        if outlet(mid)[0] > target:\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    T_out = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n    Qc, w_out, condensed = outlet(T_out)\n    return Qc, T_out, w_out, condensed, Qc - target\n\n# ============ SIMULATION ============\nrng = np.random.default_rng(7)\nh   = np.arange(HOURS)\nit_kw = (IT_MEAN + IT_AMP*np.sin(2*np.pi*(h-9)/24))*1000.0 + rng.normal(0, 15, HOURS)\ntdb   = T_MEAN + T_AMP*np.sin(2*np.pi*(h-15)/24) + rng.normal(0, 0.3, HOURS)\n\nKEYS = ['tdb','rh','twb','tcold','thot','plume_dp','mine_t','base_mu','mu_after',\n        'rec','fan_pen','pump','hp','extra','hp_on','cond_ok',\n        'plume_t','plume_w','out_t','out_w','mine_in','qc','evap','condensate','coil_resid_kw']\ncases, SUM = {}, {}\nfor name,(rhm,rha) in RH_SCHED.items():\n    rh = rhm - rha*np.sin(2*np.pi*(h-15)/24) + rng.normal(0, 1.0, HOURS)\n    d = {k: np.zeros(HOURS) for k in KEYS}\n    Tm = T_MINE0\n    for i in range(HOURS):\n        m_air = AIR_PER_MW*it_kw[i]/1000.0          # induced-draft fan schedule\n        twb   = twb_stull(tdb[i], rh[i])\n        Q     = it_kw[i]                            # IT heat to tower circuit\n        rng_K = Q/(M_WATER*CP_W)                    # tower range from heat rejection\n        tcold = twb + rng_K*(1.0-TOWER_EFF)/TOWER_EFF\n        hp = 0.0\n        if tcold + HX_APPROACH > T_FAC_LIMIT:       # passive HX insufficient -> chiller\n            lift  = tcold + HX_APPROACH - T_FAC_LIMIT\n            cop   = min(6.0, max(3.0, 6.5 - 0.25*lift))\n            hp    = Q/cop\n            Q     = Q + hp                          # compressor heat into tower circuit\n            rng_K = Q/(M_WATER*CP_W)                # recalculated once, no loop\n            tcold = twb + rng_K*(1.0-TOWER_EFF)/TOWER_EFF\n        thot = tcold + rng_K\n        w_in, Tp, w_p, Tdp = plume(tdb[i], rh[i], Q, m_air)\n        evap  = m_air*(w_p - w_in)\n        drift = DRIFT_FRAC*M_WATER\n        blow  = max(0.0, evap/(COC - 1.0) - drift)  # drift also removes dissolved solids\n        base  = evap + drift + blow\n        # ---- plume condenser on closed mine loop (non-mixing) ----\n        mine_in = Tm\n        Qc, T_out, w_out, condensate, residual = plume_condenser(Tp, w_p, Tm, m_air)\n        # Cap makeup credit at the tower's evaporation. Total condensation\n        # may include ambient humidity; this does not trace water provenance.\n        rec = min(max(0.0, evap), max(0.0, condensate))\n        Tm += (Qc - U_LOSS*(Tm - T_ROCK))*DT/(V_MINE*1000.0*CP_W)\n        fan_pen = COIL_DP*(m_air/RHO_AIR)/FAN_ETA/1000.0   # coil pressure-drop penalty, kW\n        pump    = 9.81*M_MINE*PUMP_HEAD/PUMP_ETA/1000.0\n        vals = [tdb[i],rh[i],twb,tcold,thot,Tdp,Tm,base,max(0.0,base-rec),rec,\n                fan_pen,pump,hp,fan_pen+pump+hp,float(hp>0),float(rec>0),\n                Tp,w_p,T_out,w_out,mine_in,Qc,evap,condensate,residual]\n        for k,v in zip(KEYS, vals): d[k][i] = v\n    cases[name] = d\n    it_tot  = it_kw.sum(); base_tot = d['base_mu'].sum(); rec_tot = d['rec'].sum()\n    SUM[name] = dict(save=100*rec_tot/base_tot, extra=100*d['extra'].sum()/it_tot,\n                     maxt=d['mine_t'].max(), condh=int(d['cond_ok'].sum()),\n                     hph=int(d['hp_on'].sum()), base_ml=base_tot*DT/1e6,\n                     after_ml=d['mu_after'].sum()*DT/1e6, rec_ml=rec_tot*DT/1e6,\n                     wue_b=base_tot*DT/it_tot, wue_a=d['mu_after'].sum()*DT/it_tot)\n\n# ============ OUTPUT FILES ============\nfacts = \"\".join(f\"case_result({n}, {s['save']:.1f}, {s['extra']:.1f}, {s['maxt']:.1f}, {s['condh']}).\\n\"\n                for n,s in SUM.items())\nwith open('/shared/mine_cooling.csv','w',newline='') as f:\n    wtr = csv.writer(f); wtr.writerow(['case','hour']+KEYS)\n    for name,d in cases.items():\n        for i in range(HOURS): wtr.writerow([name,i]+[round(float(d[k][i]),4) for k in KEYS])\nwith open('/shared/mine_cooling_status.pl','w') as f:\n    f.write(facts)\n\n# Refresh only the marked facts block in the named Prolog cell.\n# Keep cell names and markers unchanged when translating the workbook.\npl = nb_read('classification', '.code')\npl = pl[:pl.index('% FACTS-BEGIN')] + '% FACTS-BEGIN\\n' + facts + pl[pl.index('% FACTS-END'):]\nnb_write('classification', '.code', pl)\n\nfor name,s in SUM.items():\n    print(f\"{name}: maximum coil energy residual {np.max(np.abs(cases[name]['coil_resid_kw'])):.2e} kW\")\n    print(f\"{name}: water saved {s['save']:.0f}% (WUE {s['wue_b']:.2f}->{s['wue_a']:.2f} L/kWh), \"\n          f\"extra energy {s['extra']:.1f}%, max mine {s['maxt']:.1f}C, cond {s['condh']}h, HP {s['hph']}h\")\n",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "simulation"
      },
      {
        "code": ":- dynamic case_result/5.\n:- retractall(case_result(_, _, _, _, _)).\n% FACTS-BEGIN\n% Run simulation first: it writes this marked facts block.\n% FACTS-END\n\n% Thresholds below are illustrative teaching choices, not engineering criteria.\nclassify(Case, Class) :-\n    case_result(Case, Save, Energy, MaxT, CondH),\n    (   CondH < 8.4                       % < 5% of 168 simulated hours\n    ->  Class = no_condensation\n    ;   MaxT >= 28.0\n    ->  Class = thermal_limit\n    ;   (Save < 10.0 ; Energy > 5.0)\n    ->  Class = marginal\n    ;   Class = promising_toy_result\n    ).\n\nreport(Case) :-\n    classify(Case, Class),\n    case_result(Case, Save, Energy, _, _),\n    format(\"~w: ~w | water saving ~1f% | extra energy ~1f%~n\",\n           [Case, Class, Save, Energy]).\n\n( case_result(_, _, _, _, _)\n-> report(hot_dry), report(hot_humid)\n;  writeln(\"Run the simulation cell before this classification cell.\") ).\n",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "classification"
      },
      {
        "code": "import copy, textwrap\n\ndef _cooling_plot_layout(layout):\n    result = copy.deepcopy(layout)\n    result['height'] = 600\n    result['margin'] = {'t': 200, 'b': 180, 'l': 90, 'r': 90}\n    title = result.get('title', {})\n    if isinstance(title, str):\n        title = {'text': title}\n    title['text'] = '<br>'.join(textwrap.wrap(str(title.get('text', '')), width=45))\n    title.update({'x': 0.5, 'xanchor': 'center', 'y': 0.99, 'yanchor': 'top', 'pad': {'t': 30}})\n    result['title'] = title\n    result.setdefault('legend', {}).update({'orientation': 'v', 'x': 0, 'y': 1.12,\n                                         'xanchor': 'left', 'yanchor': 'bottom'})\n    for note in result.get('annotations', []):\n        if 'text' in note:\n            note['text'] = '<br>'.join(textwrap.wrap(str(note['text']), width=45))\n        if note.get('yref') == 'paper' and note.get('y', 0) < 0:\n            note['y'] = -0.28\n            note['yanchor'] = 'top'\n    return result\n\nhr = list(range(HOURS))\nnames = {'hot_dry': '#d62728', 'hot_humid': '#1f77b4'}\n\n# --- Chart 1: water balance comparison ---\nt1, xcats = [], ['Baseline makeup', 'After recovery', 'Recovered condensate']\nfor c in ['hot_dry', 'hot_humid']:\n    s = SUM[c]\n    t1.append({'x': xcats,\n               'y': [s['base_ml'], s['after_ml'], s['rec_ml']],\n               'type': 'bar',\n               'name': f\"{c} (save {s['save']:.0f}%, +{s['extra']:.1f}% energy)\",\n               'marker': {'color': names[c]}})\nmplot(t1, layout=_cooling_plot_layout({'barmode': 'group',\n                  'title': {'text': 'Weekly tower makeup water (10 MW IT, toy model)'},\n                  'yaxis': {'title': 'Water (ML)'},\n                  'legend': {'orientation': 'h', 'y': -0.2}}))\n\n# --- Chart 2: hourly plume dew point vs mine-water temperature ---\nt2 = []\nfor c, dash in [('hot_dry', 'solid'), ('hot_humid', 'dot')]:\n    t2.append({'x': hr, 'y': list(cases[c]['plume_dp']), 'type': 'scatter',\n               'mode': 'lines', 'name': f'{c} plume dew point (°C)',\n               'line': {'color': names[c], 'dash': dash, 'width': 2}})\n    t2.append({'x': hr, 'y': list(cases[c]['mine_t']), 'type': 'scatter',\n               'mode': 'lines', 'name': f'{c} mine water (°C)',\n               'line': {'color': names[c], 'width': 3},\n               'opacity': 0.55})\nmplot(t2, layout=_cooling_plot_layout({'height': 480, 'title': {'text': 'Condensation driving force: plume dew point vs mine water'},\n                  'xaxis': {'title': 'Hour of week'},\n                  'yaxis': {'title': 'Temperature (°C)'},\n                  'legend': {'orientation': 'v', 'x': 0, 'y': 1.02,\n                             'xanchor': 'left', 'yanchor': 'bottom'},\n                  'margin': {'t': 140, 'b': 110},\n                  'annotations': [{'xref': 'paper', 'yref': 'paper', 'x': 0, 'y': -0.32, 'yanchor': 'top',\n                                   'showarrow': False, 'font': {'size': 11},\n                                   'text': ('Toy model: results depend on weather, heat-exchanger design, '\n                                            'mine hydraulics, fan and heat-pump assumptions, and long-term '\n                                            'thermal recharge.')}]}))\n",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "dashboard"
      },
      {
        "code": "# ===== Dry-cooling comparison + upstream (source) water — reuses simulation variables =====\n# Historical/reference sources are cited in the final Markdown cell.\n# All factors and equipment efficiencies remain editable toy assumptions.\nimport numpy as np, csv\n\nANN = 52.1429            # weeks/yr — annualizes the simulated week (NOT a full-year weather run)\n\n# ---- declared toy assumptions (same IT load, heat rejection, climate, hours as wet baseline) ----\nTOWER_FAN_SP    = 125.0  # Pa induced-draft tower fan static pressure\nTOWER_PUMP_HEAD = 20.0   # m tower-loop pump head\nOVERHEAD_FRAC   = 0.05   # non-cooling facility overhead (UPS, lighting) / IT\nT_RETURN        = 37.0   # degC facility-loop return temperature\nCHILL_ETA       = 0.42   # air-cooled chiller: fraction of Carnot COP\nT_EVAP_K        = 280.0  # K chiller evaporator (~7 degC)\nCOND_APP        = 12.0   # K chiller condensing approach over ambient\nCHW_PUMP_FRAC   = 0.01   # chilled-water pump / cooling load\nDC_APPROACH     = 5.0    # K dry-cooler approach (loop supply - ambient)\nDC_FAN_FRAC     = 0.04   # dry-cooler fan power / heat rejected\nDC_PUMP_FRAC    = 0.01   # dry-cooler loop pump / heat rejected\nASSIST_ETA      = 0.40   # trim mechanical assistance: fraction of Carnot COP\nADIABATIC       = False  # optional adiabatic assist; OFF => zero direct water for dry cases\n\nGRID_WI = 4.35           # L/kWh configurable; 2023 US supplied-electricity reference (LBNL),\n                         # INCLUDES reservoir evaporation allocated to hydropower — accounting choice\nWI_CASES = {'US grid 2023 ref (incl. hydro reservoirs)': 4.35,\n            'wet-cooled natural-gas CC': 0.776, 'wet-cooled coal': 2.60,\n            'wet-cooled nuclear': 2.54, 'utility solar PV': 0.0038,\n            'wind (~0)': 0.0, 'custom local grid': 1.50}\n\nq      = it_kw                                   # kW heat rejection = IT load\nm_air  = AIR_PER_MW*q/1000.0\nhp_wet = cases['hot_dry']['hp']                  # conditional heat pump (wet system)\n\n# ---- wet baseline & mine-recovery electricity ----\ntower_fan  = TOWER_FAN_SP*(m_air/RHO_AIR)/FAN_ETA/1000.0\ntower_pump = 9.81*M_WATER*TOWER_PUMP_HEAD/PUMP_ETA/1000.0*np.ones(HOURS)\nwet_cool   = tower_fan + tower_pump + hp_wet\nmine_cool  = wet_cool + cases['hot_dry']['fan_pen'] + cases['hot_dry']['pump']  # hp unchanged\n\n# ---- 1) conventional air-cooled chiller: COP varies with ambient & lift (K) ----\nlift_ch    = (tdb + COND_APP + 273.15) - T_EVAP_K          # condensing - evaporating, K\ncop_chiller = np.clip(CHILL_ETA*T_EVAP_K/lift_ch, 2.0, 6.0)\nchiller_cool = q/cop_chiller + CHW_PUMP_FRAC*q\n\n# ---- 2) warm-water dry cooler: fan-only when ambient + approach meets loop limit ----\ndT_need  = tdb + DC_APPROACH - T_FAC_LIMIT\nfan_only = dT_need <= 0.0\nf_assist = np.clip(dT_need/(T_RETURN - T_FAC_LIMIT), 0.0, 1.0)   # share of load needing trim\ncop_assist = np.clip(ASSIST_ETA*(T_FAC_LIMIT - 2 + 273.15) /\n                     np.maximum(tdb + COND_APP - (T_FAC_LIMIT - 2), 2.0), 3.0, 10.0)\ndc_cool = (DC_FAN_FRAC + DC_PUMP_FRAC)*q + f_assist*q/cop_assist\n\nE_IT   = q.sum()                                  # kWh per simulated week\nE_over = OVERHEAD_FRAC*E_IT\nSCEN = {'wet baseline':      dict(cool=wet_cool,    w_site=SUM['hot_dry']['base_ml']),\n        'mine vapour recovery': dict(cool=mine_cool, w_site=SUM['hot_dry']['after_ml']),\n        'air-cooled chiller':  dict(cool=chiller_cool, w_site=0.0),\n        'warm-water dry cooler': dict(cool=dc_cool,   w_site=0.0)}\nif ADIABATIC:  # only when explicitly enabled\n    SCEN['air-cooled chiller']['w_site']  = 0.25*SUM['hot_dry']['base_ml']\n    SCEN['warm-water dry cooler']['w_site'] = 0.25*SUM['hot_dry']['base_ml']\n\nR = {}\nfor nm, sc in SCEN.items():\n    E_cool = sc['cool'].sum(); E_fac = E_IT + E_cool + E_over     # E_facility = PUE*E_IT\n    W_site = sc['w_site']*ANN*1e6                                 # L/yr\n    W_up   = E_fac*ANN*GRID_WI                                    # L/yr (upstream operational)\n    R[nm] = dict(cool_mwh=E_cool*ANN/1e3, fac_mwh=E_fac*ANN/1e3, pue=E_fac/E_IT,\n                 w_site=W_site/1e6, w_up=W_up/1e6, wue_site=W_site/(E_IT*ANN),\n                 wue_src=(W_site+W_up)/(E_IT*ANN),\n                 d_fac=0.0, ons_saved=0.0, inc_up=0.0, net_saved=0.0, frac_up=0.0)\nbw = R['wet baseline']\nfor nm, r in R.items():\n    if nm == 'wet baseline': continue\n    r['d_fac']      = 100*(r['fac_mwh']-bw['fac_mwh'])/bw['fac_mwh']\n    r['ons_saved']  = bw['w_site'] - r['w_site']\n    r['inc_up']     = (r['fac_mwh']-bw['fac_mwh'])*1e3*GRID_WI/1e6   # ML/yr\n    r['net_saved']  = r['ons_saved'] - r['inc_up']\n    r['frac_up']    = 100*r['inc_up']/r['ons_saved']\n\n# ---- denominator verification of the workbook's mine-recovery \"extra energy\" ----\nex_kwh = cases['hot_dry']['extra'].sum()         # coil fan penalty + mine pump + heat pump\nE_fac_mine = E_IT + mine_cool.sum() + E_over\nprint(f\"DENOMINATOR CHECK — workbook mine extra energy = {SUM['hot_dry']['extra']:.1f}% \"\n      f\"= (coil fan penalty + mine pump + heat pump) / IT electricity, simulated week\")\nprint(f\"  = {100*ex_kwh/E_fac_mine:.2f}% of facility electricity | dPUE +{ex_kwh/E_IT:.3f} \"\n      f\"| {ex_kwh*ANN/1e3:,.0f} MWh/yr on the repeated-hot-week basis\")\nprint(f\"Dry-cooler operation: fan-only {int(fan_only.sum())} h, mechanically assisted {int((~fan_only).sum())} h \"\n      f\"(of {HOURS} h); air-cooled chiller runs all {HOURS} h; dry-case direct water = 0 (adiabatic off)\\n\")\nprint(f\"COMPARISON (annualized x{ANN:.1f}; upstream at GRID_WI={GRID_WI} L/kWh, hydro-reservoir-inclusive US 2023 ref)\")\nhdr = f\"{'scenario':<23}{'coolMWh':>9}{'facMWh':>9}{'PUE':>6}{'onsiteML':>9}{'upstrML':>9}{'WUEsite':>8}{'WUEsrc':>7}{'dFac%':>7}{'shift%':>7}\"\nprint(hdr); print('-'*len(hdr))\nfor nm, r in R.items():\n    print(f\"{nm:<23}{r['cool_mwh']:>9,.0f}{r['fac_mwh']:>9,.0f}{r['pue']:>6.3f}{r['w_site']:>9,.0f}\"\n          f\"{r['w_up']:>9,.0f}{r['wue_site']:>8.2f}{r['wue_src']:>7.2f}{r['d_fac']:>7.1f}{r['frac_up']:>7.1f}\")\nprint(\"\\nNET MAKEUP-PLUS-ELECTRICITY WATER-METRIC REDUCTION VS WET BASELINE (same-weather extrapolation)\")\nfor nm, r in R.items():\n    if nm != 'wet baseline':\n        print(f\"{nm}: {r['net_saved']:.1f} ML/yr; facility energy change {r['d_fac']:+.1f}%\")\nprint(\"Lower facility energy and a lower defined water-accounting metric are separate objectives; inspect both.\")\n\nwith open('/shared/dry_cooling_hourly.csv','w',newline='') as f:\n    wtr = csv.writer(f)\n    wtr.writerow(['hour','tdb','it_kw','wet_cool_kw','mine_cool_kw','chiller_kw','chiller_cop',\n                  'drycooler_kw','assist_frac','assist_cop','fan_only'])\n    for i in range(HOURS):\n        wtr.writerow([i, round(float(tdb[i]),2), round(float(q[i]),1), round(float(wet_cool[i]),1),\n                      round(float(mine_cool[i]),1), round(float(chiller_cool[i]),1),\n                      round(float(cop_chiller[i]),2), round(float(dc_cool[i]),1),\n                      round(float(f_assist[i]),3), round(float(cop_assist[i]),2), bool(fan_only[i])])\nwith open('/shared/water_energy_summary.csv','w',newline='') as f:\n    wtr = csv.writer(f); wtr.writerow(['scenario']+list(next(iter(R.values())).keys()))\n    for nm, r in R.items(): wtr.writerow([nm]+[round(v,4) for v in r.values()])\n",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "dry_cooling"
      },
      {
        "code": "# ===== Water-energy plots: onsite vs upstream, trade-off, grid-intensity sensitivity =====\nscen_order = ['wet baseline', 'mine vapour recovery', 'air-cooled chiller', 'warm-water dry cooler']\ncolors = {'wet baseline': '#1f77b4', 'mine vapour recovery': '#2ca02c',\n          'air-cooled chiller': '#d62728', 'warm-water dry cooler': '#ff7f0e'}\n\n# --- 1) stacked onsite + upstream water ---\ntr_site = {'x': scen_order, 'y': [R[s]['w_site'] for s in scen_order], 'type': 'bar',\n           'name': 'onsite (tower makeup)', 'marker': {'color': '#1f77b4'}}\ntr_up   = {'x': scen_order, 'y': [R[s]['w_up'] for s in scen_order], 'type': 'bar',\n           'name': f'upstream electricity (@ {GRID_WI} L/kWh)', 'marker': {'color': '#9467bd'}}\nmplot([tr_site, tr_up], layout=_cooling_plot_layout({'barmode': 'stack',\n    'title': {'text': f'Annualized site makeup plus attributed electricity water (ML/yr; grid {GRID_WI} L/kWh)'},\n    'yaxis': {'title': 'Water (ML/yr)'}, 'legend': {'orientation': 'h', 'y': -0.25}}))\n\n# --- 2) water-vs-energy trade-off ---\ntr_pts = []\nfor s in scen_order[1:]:\n    r = R[s]\n    tr_pts.append({'x': [r['d_fac']], 'y': [r['net_saved']], 'type': 'scatter',\n                   'mode': 'markers+text', 'name': s, 'text': [s], 'textposition': 'top center', 'cliponaxis': False,\n                   'marker': {'color': colors[s], 'size': 16}})\ntr_pts.append({'x': [0.0], 'y': [0.0], 'type': 'scatter', 'mode': 'markers',\n               'name': 'wet baseline', 'marker': {'color': colors['wet baseline'], 'size': 14,\n               'symbol': 'x'}})\nmplot(tr_pts, layout=_cooling_plot_layout({'title': {'text': 'Trade-off: water-accounting reduction vs extra facility energy'},\n    'xaxis': {'title': 'Facility energy increase vs wet baseline (%)'},\n    'yaxis': {'title': 'Water-accounting reduction (ML/yr)'},\n    'legend': {'orientation': 'h', 'y': -0.2}}))\n\n# --- 3) sensitivity: fraction of onsite saving shifted upstream vs grid water intensity ---\nwi_sweep = [i*0.25 for i in range(21)]          # 0..5 L/kWh\ntr_s = []\nfor s in scen_order[1:]:\n    r = R[s]\n    frac = [100*((r['fac_mwh']-bw['fac_mwh'])*1e3*wi/1e6)/r['ons_saved'] for wi in wi_sweep]\n    tr_s.append({'x': wi_sweep, 'y': frac, 'type': 'scatter', 'mode': 'lines',\n                 'name': s, 'line': {'color': colors[s], 'width': 3}})\nshapes = [{'type': 'line', 'x0': v, 'x1': v, 'y0': 0, 'y1': 1, 'yref': 'paper',\n           'line': {'color': 'gray', 'dash': 'dot', 'width': 1}} for v in (0.776, 2.60, 4.35)]\nmplot(tr_s, layout=_cooling_plot_layout({'title': {'text': 'Sensitivity: makeup saving offset by attributed electricity water'},\n    'xaxis': {'title': 'Grid water intensity (L/kWh, operational consumption)'},\n    'yaxis': {'title': 'Makeup saving offset (%)', 'range': [0, 105]},\n    'shapes': shapes,\n    'annotations': [{'x': 0.776, 'y': 1.02, 'yref': 'paper', 'text': 'gas CC', 'showarrow': False, 'font': {'size': 10}},\n                    {'x': 2.60, 'y': 1.02, 'yref': 'paper', 'text': 'coal', 'showarrow': False, 'font': {'size': 10}},\n                    {'x': 4.35, 'y': 1.02, 'yref': 'paper', 'text': 'US 2023 (incl. hydro)', 'showarrow': False, 'font': {'size': 10}}],\n    'legend': {'orientation': 'h', 'y': -0.2}}))\n",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "python",
        "name": "analysis_plots"
      },
      {
        "code": "## Read the comparison as a trade-off, not a dominance claim\n\nThe simulation prints the results for the **current** assumptions; numerical conclusions are deliberately not hard-coded here. Changing the coil, reservoir, weather, loop limits, or electricity-water factor can change the ordering. The corrected condenser includes latent heat, so results from the original sensible-only calculation are not comparable.\n\n- **Energy:** the mine-recovery system adds coil fan and mine-pump electricity to the wet baseline. Both systems include the same conditional heat pump. The earlier `extra` metric includes that heat pump and is divided by IT electricity; it is **not** the incremental energy difference between recovery and the wet baseline. Use `dFac%` for a matched facility-energy comparison.\n- **Water:** `WUEsrc` is site tower makeup plus attributed electricity-generation consumption per IT kWh. The `net_saved` result is the decrease in that defined mixed accounting metric—not verified savings in total consumptive use. Tower makeup includes evaporation, drift and blowdown; blowdown return flows are not modeled. Compare both this metric and facility energy: a dry option can use more electricity yet have a lower metric than mine recovery, so neither option need dominate on both objectives.\n- **Scale and time:** annualized totals repeat the same simulated hot week approximately 52.1 times. They are not an annual weather simulation, a long-term mine forecast, or a site-specific environmental assessment.\n- **Grid sensitivity:** the plotted generation-water factors are illustrative historical references, not a prediction for a particular power contract. The 4.35 L/kWh reference includes an allocation of hydropower reservoir evaporation; boundaries and allocation choices matter.\n- **Feasibility:** a favorable toy result is not evidence of equipment feasibility. A real assessment would need a calibrated wet-coil model, pressure-drop curves, mine hydraulics and recharge, water-quality/health controls, seasonal weather, and consistent water-consumption accounting.\n\n### Reference reading and attribution\n\n- Shehabi et al., *2024 United States Data Center Energy Usage Report*, Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory/DOE: [report record](https://bies.lbl.gov/publications/2024-lbnl-data-center-energy-usage-report).\n- Macknick et al., *Operational water consumption and withdrawal factors for electricity generating technologies: a review of existing literature* (2012): [DOI 10.1088/1748-9326/7/4/045802](https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-9326/7/4/045802). Consumption and withdrawal are different quantities: the grid factors are consumption, while the site's tower makeup includes blowdown. Their sum is the explicitly defined mixed accounting metric, not total consumptive use.\n- *Water-energy tradeoffs in data centers: A case study in hot-arid climates* (2022): [DOI 10.1016/j.resconrec.2022.106194](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resconrec.2022.106194). It describes other facilities, not validation of this mine concept.\n- [EnergyPlus engineering reference, cooling coils](https://energyplus.readthedocs.io/en/latest/guides/engineering-reference/15.2-coils.html): wet-coil heat removal includes sensible and latent contributions. This workbook's energy-limited approximation is much simpler and is not an EnergyPlus model.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "conclusions"
      }
    ]
